## Summary

`areHookInputsEqual` in `packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactFiberHooks.js` compares dependencies only up to `min(prevDeps.length, nextDeps.length)`:

```js
for (let i = 0; i < prevDeps.length && i < nextDeps.length; i++) {
  if (is(nextDeps[i], prevDeps[i])) continue;
  return false;
}
return true;
```

When the deps array grows between renders, the extra entries are never compared, so the hook treats the inputs as unchanged and keeps the previous value.

## Reproduction

React 19.3.
